## 4. DATABASE SCHEMA

### Tables (summary):
- yield_units — system lookup for recipe yield/batch units (serving, piece, slice, etc.)
- selling_units — system lookup for selling format units
- profiles — extends Supabase auth.users — full_name, subscription_tier, revenuecat_user_id, onboarding_completed
- user_settings — currency, currency_symbol, default_food_cost_percent, unit_system per user
- ingredients — user ingredient library — name, purchase_price, purchase_quantity, purchase_unit (measurement_unit enum), waste_percent, notes, is_archived
- ingredient_categories — name, color — optional categorization for ingredients
- ingredient_price_history — auto-recorded on price change via trigger — old_price, new_price, change_source
- recipes — name, description, category, batch_size, batch_unit_id (FK → yield_units), target_food_cost_percent, is_archived, is_sample — NOTE: no selling_price column; selling prices live in recipe_selling_formats
- recipe_ingredients — junction: recipe_id, ingredient_id, quantity, unit (measurement_unit)
- recipe_selling_formats — one or more selling formats per recipe — name, selling_unit_id (FK → selling_units), unit_quantity, selling_price, is_default
- invoice_scans — V2 only
- invoice_scan_items — V2 only

### Enums:
- measurement_unit — kg, g, lb, oz, l, ml, fl_oz, cup, tbsp, tsp, gallon, piece, dozen, pack, other
- subscription_tier — free, hobbyist, pro
- recipe_category — starter, main, dessert, beverage, bread, sauce, snack, other

### Rules:
- Row Level Security always enabled on all tables
- Users only ever see their own data
- New user profile and settings auto created via trigger on signup
- Ingredient price changes auto tracked via trigger
- Never disable RLS
- Never use service role key in client code

