## 5. UNIT CONVERSION RULES

Units are grouped into three families:

**Weight:** kg, g, lb, oz — all interconvertible
**Volume:** l, ml, fl_oz, cup, tbsp, tsp, gallon — all interconvertible
**Count:** piece, dozen, pack, other — no conversion

Rules:
- Weight to weight: always convertible
- Volume to volume: always convertible
- Weight to volume: NOT convertible — show error to user
- Count to anything: NOT convertible — must use same unit
- If user tries to mix incompatible units — show clear error message

Calculation flow:
- Convert purchase unit to base unit (grams or ml)
- Convert recipe quantity unit to base unit
- Calculate cost per base unit from purchase price
- Multiply by recipe quantity in base units
- Apply waste percentage on top

---

## 6. COST CALCULATION LOGIC

All calculations happen in calculations.js — never in component code.

Formulas:
- ingredient_cost = (recipe_quantity / purchase_quantity) × purchase_price × unit_conversion × (1 + waste_percent / 100)
- total_recipe_cost = sum of all ingredient costs
- cost_per_serving = total_recipe_cost / batch_size
- recommended_price = cost_per_serving / (target_food_cost_percent / 100)
- actual_food_cost_percent = (cost_per_serving / selling_price) × 100
- gross_profit = selling_price − cost_per_serving
- gross_margin_percent = (gross_profit / selling_price) × 100

Margin color coding:
- Green — actual food cost % is at or below target
- Yellow — actual food cost % is within 5% above target
- Red — actual food cost % is more than 5% above target

