## 7. APP FLOW

### Onboarding (first time only):
1. Welcome screen — app name, tagline, Get Started button
2. Sign up screen — email and password
3. Supabase trigger auto creates profile and user_settings
4. Redirect to Dashboard
5. Dashboard shows pre-loaded sample recipe — Chocolate Chip Cookies
6. User sees cost calculation immediately — this is the magic moment

### Returning user:
1. App opens — check Supabase session
2. Session exists — go to Dashboard
3. No session — go to Welcome screen

### Add Ingredient flow:
1. Ingredients tab
2. Tap plus button
3. Enter name, purchase price, purchase quantity, purchase unit
4. Optional — select category, add waste percent, add notes
5. Save
6. Return to ingredient list

### Create Recipe flow:
1. Recipes tab
2. Tap plus button
3. Enter recipe name, category, batch size, batch unit, target food cost %
4. Optional — enter selling price to see actual margin
5. Add ingredients section — tap Add Ingredient
6. Select ingredient from library
7. Enter quantity used and unit
8. Real time cost preview updates as ingredients are added
9. Save recipe
10. Redirect to recipe detail screen showing full cost breakdown

### Update Ingredient Price flow:
1. Ingredients tab
2. Tap ingredient
3. Edit price
4. Save
5. All recipes containing that ingredient automatically update costs via Supabase realtime

### View Recipe Results flow:
1. Recipes tab
2. Tap recipe card
3. Recipe detail screen shows:
   - Total recipe cost
   - Cost per serving
   - Recommended selling price
   - Actual food cost % (if selling price set)
   - Gross margin % (if selling price set)
   - Margin status badge — green yellow or red
   - Full ingredient cost breakdown list

### Export PDF flow (Pro only):
1. Recipe detail screen
2. Tap Export button
3. If not Pro — show paywall
4. If Pro — generate PDF
5. Share sheet opens

### CSV Import flow (Pro only):
1. Ingredients tab
2. Tap Import button
3. If not Pro — show paywall
4. If Pro — file picker opens
5. Select CSV file
6. Column mapping screen
7. Review imported ingredients
8. Confirm — all ingredients imported

