## 9. CODING STANDARDS

### Language:
- JavaScript only — never suggest TypeScript
- ES2022+ — use optional chaining, nullish coalescing, destructuring
- Async/await always — never .then() chains
- const and let only — never var

### Components:
- Functional components only — never class components
- Default export for screens
- Named exports for reusable components
- One component per file

### Error handling:
- Every async operation in try/catch
- Always show user friendly error message — never raw Supabase errors
- Always have loading state for async operations
- Always have error state for async operations

### Lists:
- Always use FlatList for lists — never ScrollView with .map()

### Performance:
- React.memo for list item components
- useMemo for cost calculations
- useCallback for functions passed as props

### Naming:
- Components and screens — PascalCase
- Functions, variables, hooks — camelCase
- Constants — UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Files — PascalCase for components, camelCase for everything else

